+If the paddle tries to move into the boundary it becomes stationary, so it disappears from the difference image. Boundary commands are not directly penalized; a negative reward occurs only when the opponent scores. Thus we cannot assume rewards automatically solve the missing-position problem.
+
+Pong-v5 has sticky actions that can repeat the previous action regardless of the chosen action. We retained this behavior to match v5. The repeat probability is 0.25 per emulator frame, so within four frames there can be zero, one or more repetitions; it is not guaranteed that exactly one requested action is ignored. Identical reset seeds and fixed action sequences reproduced frame/reward hashes. This tests reproducibility, not that stickiness has a small effect.
