 \section{Policy Gradient with Baseline}
-A baseline is just an amount we subtract off of $G_t$ independent of the rest of the episode. This doesn't change the expectation of the gradient but changes it's variance. The right choice of baseline will reduce the variance. We can pick a constant baseline or predict an baseline based on the action and state with e.g. a neural network. For CartPole we will use a neural network and for Pong a constant.
+A baseline is just an amount we subtract off of $G_t$ that does not depend on the current action, given the information before that action. This doesn't change the expectation of the unclipped gradient estimator but changes its variance. The right choice of baseline will reduce the variance. We can pick a constant baseline or predict a baseline based on the state and time with e.g. a neural network. For CartPole we will use a neural network and for Pong a constant.
 
