+We use a new neural network with input the state and the time (divided by 500). We have a 64 node hidden layer with $\tanh$ activation functions. Then we have a single output node that tries to predict $G_t$. We update our actor model after completing our batch of 32 episodes, using detached baseline predictions from its existing weights. Afterward we train the separate baseline with 5 Adam steps at learning rate $0.01$ to minimize MSE against the observed $G_t$s. Thus current outcomes are used to fit predictions for later batches.
+
+The plot still has large changes, and the primary final model scored $260.308\pm57.013$, worse than the basic model. Four of the 500 evaluations reached 500; 496 failed physically. Theory does not guarantee a better final policy. Across three seeds, the average final scores were 323.588 with the baseline and 418.570 without it.
